:: arjun_sneak_out_d4
<<img "arjun_sneaking_out.png" "4:25 AM   the obstacle course">>
The alarm is vibration only, pressed under the pillow so the buzz transmits through cotton and foam into your skull and nowhere else. 4:25. Five minutes before you have to move.

Rohit is a geological formation. Face-down, one arm off the cot, the snore cycling through its phases   the deep rumble, the peak, the terrifying three-second silence, the resume. The Axe Dark Temptation from last night has mixed with sleep-sweat into a biological event.

You sit up slowly   weight to the rigid edge of the frame, not the traitor springs. Clothes prepped on the chair last night: jeans, t-shirt, shoes stashed //under// the bed so the pickup doesn't put you over the creaky zone. T-shirt over the head. Jeans   button, zip, belt buckle held steady so the metal doesn't clink, which in this silence would be roughly a gunshot.

Shoes in hand. Not on feet. Three metres of floor between you and the door, and on it: Rohit's gym bag (strap extended like a tripwire), the Maggi tower (one bump and it avalanches), his basketball shoes at the exact toe-catching angle.

Left foot past the gym bag. Right foot between the Maggi tower and the desk. Left foot around the basketball shoes. Hand on the handle.

The door SQUEAKS.

You freeze. Rohit mumbles. <<t "\"Bhai... Maggi...\"" "Bhai... Maggi...">>

You don't breathe. The Redmi buzzes in your pocket   Kavya: //Stop being dramatic and just OPEN it.// Rohit's mumble dissolves back into a snore. You pull the door in one motion, ripping the bandage, and slip through.

Corridor. Dark. Down the stairs, shoes on at the front door. Outside the air is cool, September's monsoon residue in the pre-dawn humidity. You walk the Pulsar fifty metres down the street before you start it   the engine carries, and the PG walls are thinner than your cover story.

The Pulsar growls to life. Headlight cutting the dark. Katraj is sleeping. You ride toward Pataleshwar.
