:: arjun_first_kavya_body_d4
<<img "arjun_first_kavya_body.png" "second morning in this body">>
You open Kavya's eyes and the world has settled into its shorter, curvier dimensions   and this time there's no lurch to it. The temple walls are above you. The ground is closer. The hair falls across your face and you push it back without thinking about it as a foreign object.

The breasts announce themselves   weight, warmth, the braless morning state where they hang free under the cotton nightie she wore to travel. Yesterday that was a klaxon. Today it's information: //bra, first thing, before anything else.//

You start the walk to the hostel. Twenty-five minutes of physics you never studied   the hips rotating, the dupatta on its schedule, the smaller stride. You're not fighting the body anymore. You're riding it. Like a hotel room on the second night: you know where the light switch is.

<div class="thought arjun">Not yours. Not close to yours. But familiar. That's a strange word for it, and it's the right one.</div>
\
<<run setup.flag("arjun_first_kavya_body_d4")>>\
<<run setup.discover("the body is starting to feel like a place, not a costume", "arjun")>>
<<hubreturn "Keep walking">>


:: arjun_pharma_read_d4
You sit on Kavya's cot with Robbins Pathology open on your knees   the eternal prop, the thing Kavya does at this hour. You actually read a page. Apoptosis: programmed, tidy, the cell shrinks and packages itself. Necrosis: the messy one, the cell swells and bursts and the neighbourhood gets inflamed.

You retain maybe forty percent. But forty percent is enough to survive a corridor quiz from Sneha, and the posture is right   this is what Kavya's body is supposed to be doing at 7 AM, not scrolling.
<<hubreturn>>


:: arjun_mirror_d4
The bathroom mirror. Kavya's face, damp from the shower, the beauty mark under the cheekbone. Yesterday you stared at this face like it was an accusation. Today you check your teeth, tuck a strand of hair, and move on.

The bra's on   your own work, first try. The kameez sits right. You look like a medical student running slightly late, which is exactly the target.

<div class="thought arjun">Twenty-one years in one body and two mornings in another, and the second one is already less strange. That should probably worry you more than it does.</div>
<<hubreturn>>


:: arjun_terrace_d4
<<img "meera_holding_d4.png" "the terrace railing, afternoon">>
You lean on the terrace railing in Kavya's body and let yourself just feel it for a minute. The warmth of the September sun on skin that reports more than yours does. The way the noise of the hostel   two hundred girls, radios, buckets   comes in through ears calibrated a notch higher.

Meera's manuscript is downstairs. Priya's at the library. The swap-back is at half five. For this one minute none of it needs anything from you.

<div class="thought arjun">Six days on the countdown now. Five after tonight. You don't let yourself think about what four means.</div>
<<hubreturn>>
